# UI Language — Company Profile

GONLINE is an Indonesian digital agency site. **Marketing copy and forms default to Indonesian.** Keep tone clear and professional.

## Applies to

- Page titles, subtitles, descriptions, SEO `title` / `description`
- Form labels, placeholders, validation & success/error messages
- Empty states, CTAs, FAQ, section headlines
- `aria-label` / `title` when user-facing
- Insight list blurbs and share UI chrome (not article body from Sheets)

## Follow existing surfaces

- **Nav** already uses short English labels (`Services`, `About`, `Insight`) — don't rename unless asked
- **Body / forms** lean Indonesian (`Pesan Terkirim!`, Insight metadata, dll.)
- When editing a page, match that page's established language — don't mix randomly in one section

## Does NOT apply to

- **Article content** from Google Sheets (title, excerpt, body) — content-owned
- **Git commits, PRs, code comments** — team preference
- **User chat** with the agent — respond in the user's language

## Locale

- Dates: prefer readable local format helpers already in `src/lib/formatDateTime.ts`
- No invented metrics, fake client counts, or fabricated testimonials

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — English form copy on an Indonesian contact flow
<h3>Message sent!</h3>

// ✅ GOOD — match ContactForm
<h3>Pesan Terkirim!</h3>
```

```ts
// ❌ BAD — inventing proof
description: "Trusted by 10,000+ brands worldwide"

// ✅ GOOD — honest positioning
description: "Solusi website, aplikasi, dan strategi digital untuk pertumbuhan bisnis."
```
